      "message": "Hello Myles, Kris,\n\nWe have done some updates in order to by-pass the build error observed due to the presence of \u0027libbt-vendor.so\u0027 on internal master:\n1. A new library android.hardware.bluetooth@1.0-impl-test is added for the sole purpose of testing bluetoothV1.0_fuzzer.\nIn android.hardware.bluetooth@1.0-impl-test, a flag \u0027BT_FUZZER\u0027 is set, which enables the dlopen of \u0027libbt-vendor-default.so\u0027 rather than \u0027libbt-vendor.so\u0027\n2. The fuzzer is also updated accordingly to create \u0027libbt-vendor-default.so\u0027 library rather than \u0027libbt-vendor.so\u0027\n\nPlease let us know if it looks fine.",
